lantern-pr 1
# 70
#title fix: Macro map is no longer drawn twice when it enters an area while mounting
#url https://github.com/MobileReality/lantern/pull/70
#branch fix/macro-single-mount
#base origin/main
#opened 2026-11-18
#head e4bceb6d4e4856b4361f8b06a9df9b41b3953767
#summary Macro map: one map instead of two stacked copies on projects with a large area
#describe what The Macro map is drawn once even when it enters an area while it is still being mounted.
#describe before On a project with a large area (mobile-reality-site-v2), opening Macro left two maps stacked at different zoom levels.
#describe after The repaint caused by entering the area is applied to the one map as an update.
#describe verified Reproduced with the real mobile-reality-site-v2 map in the graph harness (two maps before, one after); new stage test, macro e2e, typecheck and lint green.
+ test/macroview-stage.test.ts
~ src/renderer/lib/macroview/stage.ts
#order src/renderer/lib/macroview/stage.ts
#order test/macroview-stage.test.ts
#reason test/macroview-stage.test.ts Fails when a map that enters an area while mounting leaves two maps in the host
#reason src/renderer/lib/macroview/stage.ts Holds a repaint that arrives during mounting and applies it as an update, so a second map is never mounted on top
#story Opening the Macro map
#step actor Reviewer
#step action opens the Macro view of a project with one large area
#file src/renderer/lib/macroview/stage.ts
#step subject the areas map
#below interaction can read and zoom one map
#below consequence two copies of the map drawn on top of each other => one map, the area entry applied as an update
